Considered by many to be a key aspect of Sartre’s notion of radical freedom, ________ underscores personal responsibility for every action one takes.

Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", "choices": ["A) Jean-Paul Sartre, a philosopher renowned for exploring consciousness", "B) the critics discussing existential works on human liberty", "C) the moral implications he often raised in public debates", "D) Sartre’s notion of radical freedom"], "answer": "D", "explanation": "The opening phrase, “Considered by many...,” modifies the subject that follows. Because that phrase describes a “key aspect of Sartre’s notion of radical freedom,” the subject should refer to the concept under discussion rather than Sartre himself, his critics, or any other entity. Choices A, B, and C refer to people or to implications, which do not match the modifier. Choice D correctly places Sartre’s notion of radical freedom after the modifier, making the sentence logically and grammatically consistent.", "topic": "Sartre’s notion of radical freedom and responsibility"}

