corporating partially correct reasoning—would better challenge high-performing students. Minor tweaks in phrasing could also help deepen the multi-step analysis required, aligning it more perfectly with a hard-difficulty standard.", "difficulty_feedback": "While the passages use sophisticated language and the question demands a comparison of nuanced perspectives, the reasoning required isn’t as layered as typically seen in hard questions. To better match the hard-difficulty label, consider adding elements that require identifying unstated assumptions or implications. Refining the distractors to include more plausibly attractive but subtly flawed reasoning would also push the difficulty level closer to the intended challenge for top scorers."}

